      "agentRuntime": "langgraph",
      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here's how **long rests** work in Frosthaven:\n\n## Declaring a Long Rest\n\nDuring the **Card Selection** step, a character may declare a long rest instead of playing two cards. This constitutes their **entire turn** for the round and is performed on **initiative 99**.\n\n> A character must have at least two cards in their discard pile to rest.\n\n## Long Rest Steps (in order)\n\n1. **Lose one card of choice** from their discard pile and return the remaining cards to their hand. *(mandatory)*\n2. **Perform \"*Heal* 2, self\"** *(optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items** *(optional)* — items can even be used during the same turn they are recovered.\n\n## Key Points\n\n- You choose **which card to lose** (unlike a short rest, where the lost card is random).\n- The long rest happens at **initiative 99**, meaning almost everything else acts before you.\n- You play **no ability cards** on a long rest turn — it is your entire turn.\n\n*Source: Frosthaven Rulebook, passages 72 & 125*",
